Roland, on sequencing. I am less worried about the dates than about the order=
, because two of the steps are being planned in parallel when they can only h=
appen in sequence.

The consents have to be obtained before the charter amendment is filed, and t=
he filing has to be effective before the shares are issued. Everyone knows th=
at in the abstract, and yet the current timetable has the consents and the fi=
ling in the same week with no dependency shown.

Gregor and I do not disagree on any of this. The issue is that the timetable =
is a list rather than a sequence, and a list invites people to work on whatev=
er is nearest.

My suggestion is that we redraw it as three gates rather than fourteen dates.=
 Nothing in gate two starts until gate one is closed, and somebody is named f=
or closing each gate. That is a shorter document and a more honest one.

